# API routes — must come BEFORE the SPA fallback, or /* eats them.
# Kept here (instead of in netlify.toml) because Netlify's resolved order
# puts _redirects rules first and we need /api/* to win.
/api/*  /.netlify/functions/:splat  200

# WEC-303: SEO crawler endpoints. Same rationale — must come BEFORE the
# SPA fallback or Lighthouse + Googlebot get the index.html HTML when
# they ask for plain text/XML. Status 200 (not 301) so the served
# content is from the actual file at that path, not the redirect target.
/robots.txt   /robots.txt   200
/sitemap.xml  /sitemap.xml  200

# ─── TEMPORARY (2026-09-17) — WEC-790 ────────────────────────────────────
# A marketing campaign went out with https://dev--fitpal-order.netlify.app
# instead of orders.fitpal.gr. Real customers placed real orders on the dev
# deploy, which is wired to the Viva DEMO merchant and to the SAME Supabase
# database — so sandbox payments wrote "paid" onto live orders and ~108 € was
# never actually collected.
#
# Until the campaign goes cold, bounce human traffic on that hostname to
# production. Domain-level rule: the source is an absolute URL, so it matches
# ONLY that host. orders.fitpal.gr and localhost are untouched.
#
# Two carve-outs keep dev usable as a dev environment:
#   · /api/*   — already handled by the rule at the top of this file, which
#                matches on every host. Viva demo webhooks keep working.
#   · /order/* — the Viva demo success/failure return URLs registered in the
#                demo dashboard point here. Redirecting them would break the
#                dev payment flow.
#
# Developers: use the deploy permalink (<deploy-id>--fitpal-order.netlify.app),
# which is not the `dev--` host and is therefore not redirected.
#
# REMOVE THIS BLOCK once the campaign is cold.
https://dev--fitpal-order.netlify.app/order/*  /index.html  200
https://dev--fitpal-order.netlify.app/*  https://orders.fitpal.gr/:splat  302!
# ─── end temporary block ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

# SPA fallback — catch-all, last.
/*      /index.html                 200
